(The call edge against name shadowing. The list being widened is a GLOBAL;
 the call that widens it is written inside another function, which has no
 list parameter of its own; and the widening function's parameter carries
 the SAME name as the global it will be handed. The pre-scan walks each
 function body on a snapshot precisely so two same-named things keep
 opposite verdicts, so the widening has to land on the global without the
 callee's parameter of that name catching it instead. docs/BUGS_FOUND.md
 #97.)

a list called noted is [].
a list called counted is [1, 2].

To 'note whatever' with a list called noted and a text called label.
  append label to noted.

To 'add one more' with a list called counted and a number called extra.
  append extra to counted.

To 'grow the globals'.
  'note whatever' of noted and "reached the global",
  'add one more' of counted and 3.

'grow the globals'.
Print "noted last: {noted's last}".
Print "counted last: {counted's last}".
Print "counted: {counted}".
